    "false_authority": {
      "address": "0x0000c197",
      "field": "c2_append_state.record[27]",
      "observed_value": "0xfc",
      "value_byteidentical_across_three_captures": true
    },
    "gate_gap": "The linked gate proves that the implementation reloads twice from $c197 and that retry edges return to the first reload. It does not prove that $c197 remains the canonical length authority across the nested reader and the surrounding phase/rollback lifetime.",
    "root_cause": "The Link-63 correction moved retry length from volatile call scratch to reused transaction record storage, then treated that storage as canonical. On hardware the record byte is $fc, outside the admitted 1..64 range. Reloading therefore faithfully consumes a corrupted/non-authoritative value; Slot 39 cannot complete and Cutpoint 3 is never reached.",
    "why_the_prior_fix_did_not_close_the_class": "It changed where the value was reloaded from, but did not establish ownership and lifetime for the new source. The scratch-clobber mutation covered registers, not clobber of the chosen record byte itself."
  },
